From 3b7e445ec9e320a7b32134316deb76040b3fc1e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:42:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/51] B70-IP-K7: native int8 Q.K / P.V DPAS in the QSA
 kernels (B70_QSA_I8DOT)

Over an int8_per_token_head QSA cache (IP-F), B70_QSA_I8DOT=1 quantizes Q
per (token, q head) to int8 (symmetric, fp32 scale; _qsa_quant_q_kernel) and
computes S = dot(q_i8, k_i8) as an int8 x int8 -> int32 DPAS (opsPerChan 4),
then scores = S * q_scale * k_scale in fp32; P.V stays bf16. =2 also runs
P.V as int8 x int8 -> int32: P * v_scale quantized per head row of the tile
(scale = rowmax / 127). Both attn2 and split-K. Default 0 = IP-F unchanged;
bf16/fp8 caches ignore the gate. One-time log line on use. Warmup compiles
the quantizer and the I8DOT variant when the gate is on.

attn2 stores its per-tile LSE as a [BM, DC] tile masked to column 0 under
I8DOT: IGC 2.41.5 dies (SIGFPE, ZE_RESULT_ERROR_MODULE_BUILD_FAILURE) on the
1-D store when the row vector descends from the int8 DPAS layout.
